# Copy to deploy/.env and fill in real values — deploy/.env is git-ignored.
# NEVER commit real secrets to this template.
#
# Generate strong values:
#   openssl rand -base64 24   # METADATA_DB_PASSWORD, REDIS_PASSWORD
#   openssl rand -base64 32   # JWT_SECRET, ENCRYPTION_KEY (must decode to 32 bytes)
METADATA_DB_PASSWORD=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 24>
REDIS_PASSWORD=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 24>
JWT_SECRET=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 32>
ENCRYPTION_KEY=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 32>
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<your Google OAuth client id>
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<your Google OAuth client secret>
DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# Bootstrap admin — this email becomes admin at its FIRST login (auth.md §4.4):
DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=<your OIDC email>
# Optional: restrict login to these email domains (auth.md §4.3):
# DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_ALLOWLIST_DOMAINS=yourdomain.com
#
# --- Local password accounts (auth.md §5A) ---------------------------------------
# OIDC is the default, but it is NOT required: with no provider configured (leave
# the GOOGLE_* lines as placeholders) and local accounts enabled, the stack starts
# with zero external setup. The seed below is the FIRST ADMIN's ONE-TIME credential
# (the bootstrap-admin-email account above) — the app forces a password change at
# first login. Prefer the hash form in real deployments:
#   ./gradlew :modules:auth:hashPassword
# DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_LOCAL_ENABLED=true
# DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_LOCAL_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD_HASH=<paste $argon2id$... from the task>
# Plaintext alternative (zero-setup demos; never logged, always one-time):
# DATAPIPELINES_AUTH_LOCAL_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=<one-time password>
# Workspace provisioning (configuration.md §3.17; default self-serve).
# auto-per-user = every first login provisions a personal workspace (demo shape;
# also the practical choice until the workspace-creation UI ships in 022):
# DATAPIPELINES_WORKSPACES_PROVISIONING_MODE=auto-per-user
# Microsoft — single-tenant only in v1 (auth.md §11.1); uncomment the provider
# block in application.yml and the env lines in docker-compose.yml first:
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=<your Microsoft OAuth client id>
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=<your Microsoft OAuth client secret>
#
# --- Sample data (compose `demo` profile only) --------------------------------
# Nothing below is read unless you pass `--profile demo` (or use ./app.sh --demo).
# Without them the app starts exactly as it always has: both DATAPIPELINES_BOOTSTRAP_*
# keys are paths, and empty means the feature is off (configuration.md §3.18).
#
# Where the published artifacts live. There is no default: the bucket is named at
# publication time, and a built-in guess would silently load someone else's data.
# The published bucket (us-east-1; docs/deployment.md Appendix B). app.sh --demo
# defaults to this; set it here only to override (e.g. a mirror or a local build).
# SAMPLE_BASE_URL=https://datapipelines-co.s3.amazonaws.com/sample-data/mobility
# Immutable version directory under it. Any change to the data is a new version.
# SAMPLE_VERSION=v1
#
# The SELECT-only demo login. deploy/sample-data/load.sh CREATES this role on
# Postgres and MySQL with these passwords, and the bootstrap datasources file
# resolves the same values as ${VAR} placeholders — so both sides always agree.
# Generate the passwords: openssl rand -base64 24
# SAMPLE_DB_USER=dp_demo_ro
# SAMPLE_PG_PASSWORD=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 24>
# SAMPLE_MYSQL_PASSWORD=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 24>
# Root password for the demo-profile MySQL service (the loader needs it to create
# the database and the demo role; nothing else uses it).
# SAMPLE_MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=<paste output of: openssl rand -base64 24>
#
# Where the loader leaves the files the app bootstraps from. These are paths
# INSIDE the app container, on the read-only sample volume — change them only if
# you also change the compose mount.
# DATAPIPELINES_BOOTSTRAP_DATASOURCES_FILE=/srv/sample/bootstrap-datasources.yml
# DATAPIPELINES_BOOTSTRAP_EXAMPLES_FILE=/srv/sample/examples.json
#
# The §7 demo posture: every visitor gets their own workspace, and nobody can
# register a datasource of their own (an open datasource form on a public server
# is an SSRF and port-scan primitive).
# DATAPIPELINES_WORKSPACES_PROVISIONING_MODE=auto-per-user
# DATAPIPELINES_WORKSPACES_MEMBER_DATASOURCES_ENABLED=false
